# Manuscript payloads are byte-pinned: every chapter file's SHA-256 and byte
# count are recorded in its book manifest and re-verified by
# `npm run verify:manuscript`, by the test suite, and on every server load.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `true` on the authoring machine, which would rewrite LF to
# CRLF on checkout and break every one of those hashes. These files are
# therefore excluded from end-of-line conversion entirely: what is committed is
# exactly what is checked out, on every platform.
content/books/**/*.md -text

# The manifests are byte-compared too. `npm run verify:persistent` rebuilds
# `content/books/persistent/book.json` from the locked source and compares it to
# the file on disk byte for byte, so a CRLF rewrite on checkout would fail that
# check on a fresh clone. Same exclusion, same reason.
content/books/**/*.json -text

# `app/(site)/og-medallion.ts` is generated by `scripts/brand/build_brand.py` and
# byte-compared by `--check`, exactly like the manifests above. On a checkout made
# with `core.autocrlf=true` the generator's LF output and the working tree's CRLF
# disagree and the check reports the file as DIFFERING on a tree nobody has
# edited. Same exclusion, same reason.
app/(site)/og-medallion.ts -text
